# Backend Hardening Implementation Plan

This plan aims to execute four powerful mitigations to cap resource exhaustion, close authentication loopholes, and finalize the production readiness of our EC2 Web IDE.

## User Review Required

> [!CAUTION]
> As part of this plan, we will introduce a **hard limit on concurrent terminal sessions** (e.g. 3 active projects per user at any given time). We will also enforce **rate limiting** on container creation (e.g. max 5 executions per minute per user). Please confirm if these specific numbers (3 sessions, 5 requests/min) align with your expectations, or if they should be adjusted.

## Proposed Changes

---

### Security Middleware & Limits

#### [NEW] [rateLimiter.js](file:///c:/Users/het70/Desktop/latesteditor/backend/src/middleware/rateLimiter.js)
-   **Create Redis-Backed Rate Limiting:** Implement a lightweight, sliding-window rate limit using your existing `ioredis` configuration. It will track the user's `_id` and block requests exceeding maximum execution bursts to prevent Docker OOM attacks.

#### [MODIFY] [project.routes.js](file:///c:/Users/het70/Desktop/latesteditor/backend/src/routes/project.routes.js)
-   **Apply Execution Limits:** Attach the new `rateLimit` middleware strictly to our expensive endpoints: `POST /:projectId/execute` and `POST /:projectId/session/start`.

---

### Session Boundaries (session.service.js)

#### [MODIFY] [session.service.js](file:///c:/Users/het70/Desktop/latesteditor/backend/src/services/session.service.js)
-   **Cap Concurrent Containers (Max 3):** Before spinning up a new stateful workspace container, we will verify against a Redis Set (`user_sessions:{userId}`) tracking the user's active container count. If it exceeds 3 concurrent limits, the request is rejected to preserve EC2 memory.
-   **Session Set Cleanup:** Add logic to push session creation to the Redis Set, and efficiently prune it when the session dies inside `stopSession()`.

---

### Websocket Authenticity

#### [MODIFY] [terminal.ws.js](file:///c:/Users/het70/Desktop/latesteditor/backend/src/ws/terminal.ws.js)
-   **Enforce Origin Policies (Stop CSWSH):** Inject `req.headers.origin` verification inside the WebSocket handshake event. Since cookies are attached automatically by the browser, we will drop the active socket if the origin domain executing the request does not match `process.env.FRONTEND_URL` (falling back to localhost locally).

---

### File System Disk Quotas

#### [MODIFY] [filesystem.service.js](file:///c:/Users/het70/Desktop/latesteditor/backend/src/services/filesystem.service.js)
-   **Strict Content Quotas:** Cloud environments map project directories tightly to host disks. We will extend `createFile` and `updateFile` to cap maximum file upload lengths. Optionally, we'll verify rapid recursive project sizes prior to heavy directory saves to ensure malicious scripts don't bypass Docker binds to consume the host filesystem.

